  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-9eb67343-7fff-74c7-7ea8-c60d84352fbc&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;With reference to the table above, by reason of the existing building having been constructed after 5th March 2018, development is not permitted by Class AB of Part 20 of Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended). As such, the development would not constitute ‘permitted development’ and planning permission is required.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
